menu "Aliro reader example"

menu "Aliro protocol"

config SUPPORT_FAST_TRANSACTION_PHASE
    bool "Support fast transaction phase"
    default n
    help
        Enable the expedited-fast path. When disabled, the reader uses the
        expedited-standard path and proceeds through AUTH1 before EXCHANGE.

config SUPPORT_KEYSLOT
    bool "Support credential public key lookup by key slot"
    default n
    help
        Allow the user device to return a credential key slot instead of the
        full credential public key. The example resolves the configured test
        credential public key from that key slot.

choice READER_CERT_POLICY
    prompt "Reader certificate delivery"
    default READER_CERT_POLICY_DO_NOT_SEND
    help
        Select how the reader certificate is used during expedited-standard
        authentication. The Aliro protocol allows the certificate to be sent
        with LOAD CERT, included in AUTH1, or omitted when the user device can
        authenticate the reader public key by other provisioned context.

    config READER_CERT_POLICY_SEND_VIA_LOAD_CERT
        bool "Send reader certificate via LOAD CERT"
        help
            Send the compressed reader certificate in a LOAD CERT command before
            AUTH1. This matches the default example flow.

    config READER_CERT_POLICY_SEND_VIA_AUTH1
        bool "Send reader certificate via AUTH1"
        help
            Include the compressed reader certificate in AUTH1 instead of sending a
            separate LOAD CERT command.

    config READER_CERT_POLICY_DO_NOT_SEND
        bool "Do not send reader certificate"
        help
            Do not send a reader certificate. Use this only when the user device can
            verify the reader signature through a previously provisioned reader key
            or equivalent installation-specific trust context.

endchoice # choice READER_CERT_POLICY

config SUPPORT_MAILBOX
    bool "Support mailbox exchange after expedited phase"
    default n
    help
        After expedited authentication, issue an EXCHANGE command carrying
        mailbox read/write/set requests before the normal EXCHANGE command.

config SUPPORT_STEPUP_PHASE
    bool "Support step-up phase"
    default n
    help
        After expedited-standard authentication, send an ENVELOPE command to
        enter the step-up phase and use step-up crypto for following EXCHANGE
        commands. Fast transactions skip this step-up ENVELOPE.

endmenu # menu "Aliro protocol"

endmenu # menu "Aliro reader example"
